  "notes": "An ichidan verb describing something expanding or puffing up. The physical sense of swelling extends metaphorically to describe a person puffing out their cheeks in displeasure.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {風船|ふうせん}が{膨|ふく}れる: a balloon inflates\n- {餅|もち}が{膨|ふく}れる: mochi puffs up\n- ほっぺたを{膨|ふく}れる: to puff out one's cheeks\n- {費用|ひよう}が{膨|ふく}れる: expenses swell\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {膨|ふく}らむ: also means to swell or expand, and is largely interchangeable with {膨|ふく}れる in the physical sense, but {膨|ふく}らむ tends to describe gradual, natural expansion (hopes swelling, buds swelling) while {膨|ふく}れる more readily carries the negative connotation of sulking\n- {腫|は}れる: to swell due to injury or inflammation, not general expansion",
